{"book":9,"chapter":7,"context":{"chapter":7,"title":"Hitherto Hath the Lord Helped","summary":"After twenty years Samuel calls Israel to put away their idols. At Mizpeh they fast and confess; when the Philistines attack, the Lord thunders and Israel wins. Samuel sets up a stone named Ebenezer and judges Israel for the rest of his life.","background":"'Ebenezer' means 'stone of help' (v. 12). It is the same name as the place where Israel lost the ark (4:1), so the defeat is now answered by a victory. Samuel served as judge, prophet and intercessor, traveling a yearly circuit to Bethel, Gilgal and Mizpeh before returning home to Ramah (vv. 16–17).","customs":[{"term":"Drew water and poured it out","verses":"7:6","note":"A rite not found elsewhere; it seems to express humbling and repentance before the Lord, together with fasting and confession."}],"watchFor":["Repentance comes before rescue (vv. 3–4).","Samuel prays and offers while the Lord fights (vv. 9–10).","'Hitherto hath the Lord helped us' (v. 12)."],"connections":["1 Samuel 4:1","Joshua 24:23","Judges 10:16","Psalms 99:6"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיָּבֹאוּ","vaiyavo'u","H935","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they came"],["אַנְשֵׁי","'anshei","H582","HNcmpc","[the] people of"],["קִרְיַת","kiryat","H7157","HNpl","Kiriath"],["יְעָרִים","ye'arim","H7157","HNpl","Jearim"],["וַיַּעֲלוּ","vaiya'alu","H5927","Hc/Vhw3mp","and they took up"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["אֲרוֹן","'aron","H727","HNcmsc","[the] ark of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["וַיָּבִאוּ","vaiyavi'u","H935","Hc/Vhw3mp","and they brought"],["אֹתוֹ","'oto","H853","HTo/Sp3ms","<obj.> it"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["בֵּית","beit","H1004","HNcmsc","[the] house of"],["אֲבִינָדָב","'avinadav","H41","HNpm","Abinadab"],["בַּגִּבְעָה","bagiv'ah","H1389","HRd/Ncfsa","on the hill"],["וְאֶת","ve'et","H853","HC/To","and <obj.>"],["אֶלְעָזָר","'el'azar","H499","HNpm","Eleazar"],["בְּנוֹ","beno","H1121","HNcmsc/Sp3ms","son his"],["קִדְּשׁוּ","kides